[list]
[*]Allow removing items is now held off on every stand in service, including stands that already had it switched on. A stand that reached service with it on stayed open to every colonist's outfit optimizer, which could take the uniform and wear it as everyday clothes, and an assigned owner never prevented that. The setting is now cleared when a save loads and again whenever a stand goes back into service, so a stand cannot be left exposed by accident. The automated suite that runs before every release covers this now, in both directions.
[*]The toggle's description says something useful about getting things out again. To take a garment back, use the eject button beside it in the stand's Contents tab, which drops it next to the stand. The old text told you to set the stand aside to unlock the toggle, which stopped being true the moment you put the stand back to work.
[*]Reworded the in-game text after feedback on the writing style. Same information, plainer punctuation.
[/list]
